    "description": "What: an engine's heat at night (CE-4658, thermal drivers TD-S2; docs/designs/thermal/DESIGN_Thermal_Drivers.md \u00a74e). On basic-desert at 00:30 local, clear sky, 'Observer' at (50, 300) \u2014 the thermal observer (TKB 215: a hand-held thermal sight 1500 m that resolves a signature >= 0.3; his eyes reach ~125 m at night and a standing tank makes no sound) \u2014 watches two T-72s ~500 m east, 200 m apart, on the terrain (basic-desert is 600 m square): 'Idling Tank' at (550, 250), crewed, its engine idling (a crewed vehicle starts Idle), and 'Parked Tank' at (550, 450), authored HeatSource Off (parked, engine cold). Judge: he remembers ONE contact \u2014 the idling tank (0.2 + 0.4 x 0.8 = 0.52); the cold hull (its base 0.2) never becomes a second contact. Fail: no contact, or a second one. Red-proof: author the parked tank Idle and the second contact appears.",
